Q: MongoDB: what is the difference between $elemMatch and $and to find objects inside array? A: <p>components collection:</p>
<pre class="lang-json prettyprint-override"><code>[
  {&quot;name&quot;:&quot;a&quot;, 
    &quot;items&quot;:[{&quot;quantity&quot;: 2, &quot;version&quot;: 1},{&quot;quantity&quot;: 1, &quot;version&quot;: 7}]
  },
  {&quot;name&quot;:&quot;b&quot;,
    &quot;items&quot;:[{&quot;quantity&quot;: 2, &quot;version&quot;: 3},{&quot;quantity&quot;: 1, &quot;version&quot;: 1}]
  },
  {&quot;name&quot;:&quot;c&quot;,
    &quot;items&quot;:[{&quot;quantity&quot;: 3, &quot;version&quot;: 5},{&quot;quantity&quot;: 2, &quot;version&quot;: 1}]
  },
  {&quot;name&quot;:&quot;d&quot;,
    &quot;items&quot;:[{&quot;quantity&quot;: 5, &quot;version&quot;: 2},{&quot;quantity&quot;: 7, &quot;version&quot;: 3}]
  },
  {&quot;name&quot;:&quot;e&quot;,
    &quot;items&quot;:[{&quot;quantity&quot;: 2, &quot;version&quot;: 2},{&quot;quantity&quot;: 2, &quot;version&quot;: 1}]
  },
  {&quot;name&quot;:&quot;f&quot;,
    &quot;items&quot;:[{&quot;quantity&quot;: 1, &quot;version&quot;: 1}]
  },
  {&quot;name&quot;:&quot;g&quot;,
    &quot;items&quot;:[{&quot;quantity&quot;: 3, &quot;version&quot;: 5}]
  },
  {&quot;name&quot;:&quot;h&quot;,
    &quot;items&quot;:[{&quot;quantity&quot;: 2, &quot;version&quot;: 1},{&quot;quantity&quot;: 2, &quot;version&quot;: 1}]
  }
]
</code></pre>
<hr />
<h4>$elemMatch</h4>
<p><strong>$elemMatch</strong> returns only elements that match the criteria, that is, all components having at least one item with theses properties: {&quot;quantity&quot;:1,&quot;version&quot;:1}</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>db.components.find({items: {$elemMatch: {&quot;quantity&quot;: 1, &quot;version&quot;:1}}}).count();
//returns 2
//components &quot;b&quot; and &quot;f&quot;
</code></pre>
<hr />
<h4>$and</h4>
<p><strong>$and</strong> returns only elements that has one item with quantity=1, plus another item with version=1, or the same item having both properties = 1.<br />
In summary, the component needs to have at least one item having quantity=1 and another containing version=1</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>db.components.find({$and: [{&quot;items.quantity&quot;: 1}, {&quot;items.version&quot;:1}]}).count();
//same as
db.components.find({&quot;items.quantity&quot;: 1, &quot;items.version&quot;:1}).count();
//returns 3
//components &quot;a&quot;, &quot;b&quot;, &quot;f&quot;
</code></pre>
<hr />
<h4>$or</h4>
<p><strong>$or</strong> returns all elements containing at least one item having quantity=1 or version=1<br />
If only one item contains the property quantity=1, but none containing version=1, its enough, and vice-versa.</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>db.components.find({$or: [{&quot;items.quantity&quot;: 1}, {&quot;items.version&quot;:1}]}).count();
//returns 6
//components &quot;a&quot;, &quot;b&quot;, &quot;c&quot;, &quot;e&quot;, &quot;f&quot;, &quot;h&quot;
//only &quot;d&quot; and &quot;g&quot; don't have any item with quantity=1 or version=1
</code></pre>
<blockquote>
<p>be careful with the syntax:<br />
db.components.find({$or: [{&quot;items.quantity&quot;: 1}, {&quot;items.version&quot;:1}]}).count();<br />
has different meaning of:<br />
db.components.find({$or: [{&quot;items.quantity&quot;: 1, &quot;items.version&quot;:1}]}).count();</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h4>$elemMatch using 1 criteria</h4>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>db.components.find({&quot;items.quantity&quot;: 1}).count();
//same as
db.components.find({items: {$elemMatch: {&quot;quantity&quot;: 1}}}).count()

db.components.find({&quot;items.version&quot;: 1}).count();
//same as
db.components.find({items: {$elemMatch: {&quot;version&quot;: 1}}}).count()
</code></pre>
